  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-law-thesis-review",
      "text": "A DeepSeek Harness **skill plugin** that reviews student law theses (国际经济法/法学论文) and outputs a Word review draft with **tracked changes + Word comments**."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "- Reads a student Word (.docx) thesis (single file or a folder).\n- Checks against a bundled common-issue checklist (硕士/本科自查清单合并版 + 国际经济法/法学论文高发问题).\n- Applies definite fixes as **Word tracked changes** (w:ins / w:del).\n- Writes **Word comments** for issues the student must handle themselves (overall section problems, missing basis/clarification, etc.).\n- Emits a short, objective overall review + a fix list."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install (local / from npm)",
      "text": "~~~bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "local path",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add link:D:/Coding/Creating/dsh-law-thesis-review"
    },
    {
      "section": "or from npm (once published)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add @signalight/dsh-law-thesis-review\n~~~\n\nRestart the web profile. The skill is then auto-discovered; trigger it with phrases like “批改学生论文”, “审阅这篇论文”, “以修订+批注检查论文”."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "The skill runs the bundled script:\n\n~~~bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "1) extract text + paragraph indices",
      "text": "python skills/iet-law-thesis-review/scripts/review_docx.py extract 论文.docx --out ./work"
    },
    {
      "section": "2) review: apply tracked edits + comments from a spec",
      "text": "python skills/iet-law-thesis-review/scripts/review_docx.py review 论文.docx --spec spec.json --out 论文_审查稿.docx [--author \"教师名\"]\n~~~\n\nSpec shape shown in `skills/iet-law-thesis-review/examples/spec-template.json`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- **Self-contained**: `apply_edits.py` / `models.py` / `add_comment.py` are vendored; the skill does **not** require an external word-docx plugin.\n- Checklist is **bundled** (`skills/iet-law-thesis-review/references/checklist.md`); no dependency on any local Obsidian vault path.\n- The output preserves the original title and any student info; revision/comment author defaults to the local Office/WPS username or can be set via `--author`.\n- Word: open the `_审查稿.docx` to see the redline + comment bubbles."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    },
    {
      "section": "Thesis level",
      "text": "The skill detects the paper level and routes to the matching checklist:\n\n- Undergraduate thesis -> references/checklist-undergraduate.md (with format/editing checks)\n- Master's thesis -> references/checklist-master.md (with format/editing checks)\n- Academic training / term paper -> references/checklist-academic-training.md (no format requirements)\n- Level unspecified -> references/checklist.md (general requirements only; no format nitpicks)"
    }
  ],
